  "script": "Beavers live in freshwater ecosystems such as rivers, streams, lakes and ponds. In Europe, beavers were reduced to fragmented populations with combined numbers estimated across regions. The concept became popular in conservation and was deployed in a range of contexts. This was mobilized to engender support for conservation especially where human activities damaged ecosystems. In addition, wolves often kept animals from grazing in riparian areas across the region. This protected beavers from having their vital food sources encroached upon by herbivores. The connectivity of streams to their adjacent floodplain plays an important role. Stream restoration aims to improve the environmental health of a river or stream.",
